    "question": {
      ":question/id": "09af2bfe-f934-5754-bda0-597b90d46f7a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-3)\\cdot R_{1}$ on $B?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-3)\\cdot R_{1}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-3)\\cdot R_{1}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 6+(-3)(6) & 2+(-3)(7) & -1+(-3)(5) & -3+(-3)(3)\\end{array}\\right]}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -12 & -19 & -16 & -12\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
